ht  [Applause]  all right so uh so wrapping up  um  so wrapping up here I just you know in  summary you'll say that you know the  inspection you know we're an ex Vivo  gene therapy  um company  um we had two products and two sites  that were inspected  um the agencies that were involved were  sieber otat and uh you know dmpq  division  it was a pli and a GMP inspection as I  said inspection learnings there was  extensive use of IRS for facility  information  then step foot in the facility  um it reminds me of  like I don't know if I said this before  but it reminds me of  back in the early days of  when you we had  um  protein Therapeutics and we had  monoclonal antibodies in the early days  of protein Therapeutics and monoclonal  antibodies the agency asked for  everything they asked for a lot of  information and this is reminding me  gene therapy is reminding me of the same  thing that they're sort of going back in  time and they're asking for everything  um so that's where it would be helpful  to get some more guidance from the  agency about what they're looking for  but it reminds me of that whether  they're just asking for everything Sops  all this information the facilities Etc  so the in-depth facility information and  and particularly they're also asking  because of covid right now because of  the pandemic you know raw materials and  Supply constraints  um the other things we learned is um  it's been very challenging with the  um during the pandemic with the travel  restrictions the restrictions that the  facilities themselves and then having  the need to you know replace uh  face-to-face meetings with virtual  meetings that was a  that was a challenge it was a new way of  working for a lot of us and uh and that  presented a lot a lot of challenges it  was just hard not being able to go to  the facility as often as we would like  to and engage with them  um the other thing that  occurred during this pandemic is  absenteeism it could have been  absenteeism due to you know people being  sick and being being out sick or  absenteeism also because we had a lot of  high turnover during in the industry at  the time so the the call out here is  that  you know going into all of this has had  identified who your team is and then  identify the backups and the backups of  the backups because you definitely don't  know when you're going to need them and  you want to have that all planned out  ahead of time so so really  um build out your team and then and then  know who the backups are and who the  backup backups are  um so that when you have either turnover  or you have people who are sick or out  um you can quickly pivot and adapt so  um and the problems that we're seeing I  believe that the FDA is seeing the same  thing so the challenge is that we're  seeing with turnover the challenges  we're seeing with um covid absenteeism  the agency is seeing as well and that  may be  that may be influencing some of the  questions that they're asking us because  you may be getting new reviewers  involved and Etc but anyway it's just  something to think about  um and that really that's that's about  it so  um so I want to thank you for your time  and uh I'll pause here and um take any  questions that you have and uh thank you
 

